body:
`fieldTypeToTs()` appends `[]` when `multiple` is true even if the base mapping is already an array type (e.g. `multiselect: 'string[]'` or `vector: 'number[]'`), producing `string[][]` / `number[][]`. Make the array handling consistent (e.g., represent all bases as scalars and only apply `multiple`, or detect an existing array base and avoid double-wrapping).
```suggestion

  if (!multiple) {
    return base;
  }

  // Avoid double-wrapping when the base type is already an array (e.g. "string[]" or "number[]").
  if (base.endsWith('[]')) {
    return base;
  }

  return `${base}[]`;
```
